<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Humbert I, Count of Savoy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 1047</span> · Also known as Humbert White-Hands, Humbert the White-Handed</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Humbert I, known as White-Hands, was a noble of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arles">Arles</a> who held lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurienne">Maurienne</a> and Savoy from about 1003. He gained control of Alpine passes and was rewarded by Emperor Conrad II for his support. He is regarded as the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-savoy">House of Savoy</a>, which later ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/humbert-i-count-of-savoy.jpg" alt="Humbert I, Count of Savoy" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pelagio Palagi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Comte_Humbert_I_de_Savoie.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
